1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[English subtitles are available]

2
00:00:01,180 --> 00:00:07,120
When this is all over,

3
00:00:08,710 --> 00:00:21,030
will I be able to see you?

4
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:27,890
Fali, everything is ready.

5
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:30,090
We can start the evacuation
of the Kawas now.

6
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:45,230
[Dongli]

7
00:00:47,950 --> 00:00:49,980
Good morning, everyone.

8
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:52,090
Good morning.

9
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:52,970
Mountain Travel

10
00:00:53,060 --> 00:00:57,590
has specially prepared
this special tour for you.

11
00:00:57,680 --> 00:01:01,060
Thank you all for coming.

12
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:05,200
I'm the travel planner in charge,

13
00:01:05,290 --> 00:01:10,920
as well as your guide, Hsieh Tien-ti.

14
00:01:11,890 --> 00:01:13,210
I'm Pu.

15
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:15,010
I'm Yi-han,

16
00:01:15,140 --> 00:01:16,289
the cute one.

17
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:17,520
She's so cute!

18
00:01:17,610 --> 00:01:19,410
I look forward to working with you.

19
00:01:19,539 --> 00:01:20,860
Nice to meet you.

20
00:01:20,950 --> 00:01:23,150
We'll get going then.

21
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:25,660
Go!

22
00:01:47,530 --> 00:01:48,320
Your name?

23
00:01:48,410 --> 00:01:49,590
Tinooy.

24
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:51,180
Share the blessings.

25
00:01:51,710 --> 00:01:52,539
Your name?

26
00:01:52,670 --> 00:01:53,910
Tangfol.

27
00:01:53,990 --> 00:01:55,450
Share the blessings.

28
00:01:57,030 --> 00:01:58,039
Your name?

29
00:01:58,130 --> 00:01:59,100
Kowal.

30
00:01:59,190 --> 00:02:00,640
Share the blessings.

31
00:02:02,270 --> 00:02:03,230
Your name?

32
00:02:03,630 --> 00:02:04,990
Kadofah.

33
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:06,450
Share the blessings.

34
00:02:06,970 --> 00:02:07,810
Your name?

35
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:28,010
Ms. Tien-ti.

36
00:02:28,090 --> 00:02:28,840
Yes.

37
00:02:28,930 --> 00:02:30,600
Let's take a picture together.

38
00:02:30,690 --> 00:02:32,270
Of course.

39
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,079
Come on.

40
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:36,320
-Wu Yi-han, let's take a photo.
-Let's take photos.

41
00:02:41,290 --> 00:02:42,520
'Aresing?

42
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:44,150
Your name?

43
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:46,260
'Aresing.

44
00:02:47,230 --> 00:02:48,600
Share the blessings.

45
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:50,000
Share the blessings.

46
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:53,610
Have a safe trip.

47
00:02:58,410 --> 00:02:59,070
Your name?

48
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:01,090
Onsing.

49
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:02,720
Share the blessings.

50
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:04,260
Your name?

51
00:03:04,790 --> 00:03:06,150
Damay.

52
00:03:06,990 --> 00:03:08,310
Share the blessings.

53
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:09,720
Cariwciw.

54
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:12,000
Share the blessings.

55
00:03:12,220 --> 00:03:13,500
Share the blessings.

56
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:16,930
Banai.

57
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:19,530
Take good care of yourself.

58
00:03:20,890 --> 00:03:21,860
Don't be sad.

59
00:03:25,770 --> 00:03:28,590
What am I saying? Why would you be sad?

60
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:30,700
You should be happy.

61
00:03:30,790 --> 00:03:32,070
Because after I leave,

62
00:03:32,150 --> 00:03:34,000
you will no longer be a Sikawasay.

63
00:03:34,090 --> 00:03:35,810
You won't be stuck

64
00:03:35,890 --> 00:03:37,570
in this small community.

65
00:03:37,650 --> 00:03:39,500
Then you can go to Taipei
and look for Tien-ti.

66
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:42,360
Banai.

67
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:47,160
I know you must hate me.

68
00:03:48,570 --> 00:03:51,730
You must hate me
for choosing you to be a Sikawasay.

69
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:53,579
Because of that,

70
00:03:53,670 --> 00:03:55,870
your family went through so much trouble.

71
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:57,280
You must be thinking

72
00:03:57,370 --> 00:03:59,040
that if you weren't a Sikawasay,

73
00:03:59,170 --> 00:04:02,120
you would've been able to live
the life you want.

74
00:04:02,210 --> 00:04:04,140
You could've left this tribe.

75
00:04:05,510 --> 00:04:07,660
You wouldn't have to see me again.

76
00:04:08,450 --> 00:04:09,510
Cariwciw.

77
00:04:16,110 --> 00:04:17,029
Banai.

78
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:20,290
Do you know what that annoying messenger

79
00:04:20,420 --> 00:04:22,220
told me the other day?

80
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:24,290
He found out that

81
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:26,580
I wished to go against Kakarayan's will

82
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:28,340
and continue to stay by your side.

83
00:04:28,910 --> 00:04:30,890
But that's not allowed.

84
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:32,480
So at that time,

85
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:34,280
he gave me two options.

86
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:36,350
The first is to take me away immediately.

87
00:04:36,790 --> 00:04:39,600
The second is for me
to follow Kakarayan's will

88
00:04:39,690 --> 00:04:40,880
and leave this place.

89
00:04:42,070 --> 00:04:43,780
But if I had known saying goodbye to you

90
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,900
would make me so sad,

91
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:48,840
I would've let him
take me back right away.

92
00:04:48,930 --> 00:04:49,810
Cariwciw.

93
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:53,640
You're leaving.

94
00:04:55,270 --> 00:04:56,980
Why do you still have so much to say?

95
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:11,240
Thank you.

96
00:05:13,090 --> 00:05:15,200
Thank you for always being there for me.

97
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:32,010
Banai.

98
00:05:36,850 --> 00:05:37,900
I'm going.

99
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:39,750
Take care.

100
00:07:03,610 --> 00:07:04,230
[Ms. Hsieh.]

101
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:06,290
[I'll leave the contract
and the key to you.]

102
00:07:06,380 --> 00:07:07,970
Okay. If there are any further questions,

103
00:07:08,050 --> 00:07:09,330
call me anytime.

104
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:10,340
-Congratulations.
-Thank you.

105
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:11,660
I'm leaving. Bye.

106
00:07:11,750 --> 00:07:12,670
Bye.

107
00:07:42,990 --> 00:07:44,090
What are you typing?

108
00:07:44,790 --> 00:07:46,820
My schedule. What about it?

109
00:07:48,490 --> 00:07:49,460
It's nothing.

110
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:50,730
Ting-yi invited me
to pay respects to Yue Lao.

111
00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:51,659
Do you want to come along?

112
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:54,470
Yue Lao?

113
00:07:55,659 --> 00:07:57,159
It's fine. I don't want to go.

114
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:58,740
You don't want to go?

115
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:02,300
I thought you were into these things.

116
00:08:03,890 --> 00:08:05,470
That's in the past.

117
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:10,840
Are you really the Hsieh Tien-ti

118
00:08:10,930 --> 00:08:16,560
who loves to thank God for everything?

119
00:08:16,690 --> 00:08:18,360
Fine. Whatever you say.

120
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:21,310
Wu Yi-han, don't pay respects to Yue Lao.

121
00:08:22,190 --> 00:08:24,830
I'm thinking of finding

122
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:26,410
a nice restaurant later

123
00:08:27,030 --> 00:08:29,190
and watching a movie afterward.

124
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:30,290
Come with me.

125
00:08:34,030 --> 00:08:35,610
The place I want to go

126
00:08:35,740 --> 00:08:39,570
is a Korean restaurant with handsome guys.

127
00:08:40,890 --> 00:08:41,730
What are you waiting for? Let's go.

128
00:08:41,809 --> 00:08:42,960
What do you mean?
I'm not waiting for anything.

129
00:08:43,049 --> 00:08:43,789
What are you waiting for?

130
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:44,320
Come on.

131
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:46,040
I'm hungry.

132
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:46,960
I'm hungry.

133
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:56,070
[Mountain Travel]

134
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:50,570
I'm hungrier than you.

135
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:52,110
I'm the hungriest.

136
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,870
I'm the most famished of all.

137
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,630
I'm super famished.

138
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:57,960
I'm extraordinarily famished.

139
00:08:58,050 --> 00:08:59,110
You can't continue, right?

140
00:08:59,190 --> 00:09:02,050
I'm super duper, incredibly hungry.

141
00:09:02,140 --> 00:09:02,850
How's that?

142
00:09:02,930 --> 00:09:04,910
I'm positively ravenous...

143
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,380
You really didn't erase her memory?

144
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:09,800
No.

145
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:12,440
If you didn't erase her memory,

146
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:14,810
why didn't she beg you to spare her life?

147
00:09:14,900 --> 00:09:16,220
And now,

148
00:09:16,350 --> 00:09:17,060
it seemed like nothing

149
00:09:17,190 --> 00:09:18,600
had happened.

150
00:09:18,730 --> 00:09:19,830
Look at her all delighted,

151
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:21,320
going to eat with her friend.

152
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:27,040
I can see a person's future.

153
00:09:27,130 --> 00:09:28,190
It doesn't mean

154
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:29,950
that I know what she's thinking.

155
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:32,240
Stop pretending.

156
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,290
There's nothing

157
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:34,390
you don't know.

158
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:37,030
You are 'Orad.

159
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:41,830
What a crappy ending.

160
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:44,070
Now, I feel empty after watching it.

161
00:09:44,730 --> 00:09:46,140
I should have watched another one.

162
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:48,600
Listen, the other one is worse.

163
00:09:48,690 --> 00:09:49,700
You've seen it?

164
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:52,920
I watched it three times last week.

165
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:57,800
What?
You watched the same movie three times?

166
00:09:58,240 --> 00:09:59,870
The dating app I'm using

167
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,200
introduced me to three nice guys.

168
00:10:02,290 --> 00:10:04,880
But they all asked me
to watch the same movie.

169
00:10:04,970 --> 00:10:06,950
I'm really impressed.

170
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:10,560
You watched it three times for a date.

171
00:10:10,650 --> 00:10:11,970
But the worst part is

172
00:10:12,050 --> 00:10:13,110
I've already seen it

173
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:14,830
and I had to act like
it was my first time.

174
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:16,410
I knew what the joke was going to be,
but I had to laugh anyway.

175
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:19,180
[When I close my eyes,]

176
00:10:19,310 --> 00:10:21,070
things of the future

177
00:10:21,160 --> 00:10:24,020
will play before me like reflections.

178
00:10:24,110 --> 00:10:25,210
These are all reflections

179
00:10:25,300 --> 00:10:26,840
that Kakarayan has arranged beforehand.

180
00:10:28,250 --> 00:10:29,740
As the messenger,

181
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:31,720
I'm only carrying out

182
00:10:32,780 --> 00:10:34,270
the reflections one by one.

183
00:10:36,470 --> 00:10:37,750
Aunt Su-chen.

184
00:10:39,510 --> 00:10:40,390
Have a seat inside.

185
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:43,600
Here.

186
00:10:44,750 --> 00:10:46,730
Aunt Su-chen, what brings you here?

187
00:10:47,830 --> 00:10:48,790
I got it.

188
00:10:48,880 --> 00:10:50,900
You're helping with the move, right?

189
00:10:50,990 --> 00:10:51,920
Don't worry.

190
00:10:52,050 --> 00:10:54,120
I've already taken care of my best friend.

191
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:57,770
You're moving?

192
00:10:58,690 --> 00:10:59,840
Why are you moving?

193
00:11:00,140 --> 00:11:01,160
She got a new house.

194
00:11:02,610 --> 00:11:04,630
Her house is huge and gorgeous.

195
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:06,920
I'll invite you
to the housewarming party next time.

196
00:11:08,770 --> 00:11:09,960
Where is the house?

197
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:11,980
Buying a house is a big deal.

198
00:11:12,070 --> 00:11:13,390
Why didn't you tell me?

199
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:41,240
[You're always busy working.]

200
00:11:41,370 --> 00:11:43,170
I reckon you won't go see a doctor.

201
00:11:43,260 --> 00:11:45,460
That's why I prepared

202
00:11:45,550 --> 00:11:47,180
these herbal tonic and supplement for you.

203
00:11:47,310 --> 00:11:49,820
Don't forget to drink it
before it gets cold.

204
00:11:49,910 --> 00:11:52,940
Take this one in the morning and at night.

205
00:11:53,070 --> 00:11:53,820
Remember to drink it.

206
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:17,540
Calling for my former guardian angel.

207
00:12:18,730 --> 00:12:20,840
Can you hear me?
Please answer me if you can.

208
00:12:30,650 --> 00:12:32,190
If you don't come out,

209
00:12:32,410 --> 00:12:34,210
I'll go buy alcohol.

210
00:12:35,220 --> 00:12:39,010
Then I'll get drunk and summon you.

211
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:46,440
I told you.

212
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:48,910
Don't use drinking as an excuse
to look for me.

213
00:12:49,610 --> 00:12:51,370
What if I'm not the one who shows up?

214
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:53,920
How else can I find you?

215
00:12:57,840 --> 00:12:58,630
What's the matter?

216
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:04,920
[This place is very big.]

217
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:06,550
Yes.

218
00:13:06,680 --> 00:13:07,700
You haven't unpacked.

219
00:13:09,410 --> 00:13:11,260
I'll help you clean up sometime.

220
00:13:11,830 --> 00:13:12,620
It's okay.

221
00:13:17,070 --> 00:13:18,690
You haven't drunk the soup.

222
00:13:18,830 --> 00:13:20,500
I drank a little bit.

223
00:13:20,590 --> 00:13:23,230
Put the leftover in the fridge, okay?

224
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:26,390
This thing

225
00:13:27,490 --> 00:13:28,860
is not cheap, isn't it?

226
00:13:28,950 --> 00:13:30,180
Do you have enough money?

227
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:30,970
Yes.

228
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:32,730
I'll transfer the money to you.

229
00:13:32,820 --> 00:13:33,920
I'll pay for it.

230
00:13:34,010 --> 00:13:35,410
It's okay. I have money.

231
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:37,220
Don't mention it. It's on me.

232
00:13:37,310 --> 00:13:38,930
Aunt Su-chen, don't be like this.

233
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:43,070
I didn't want to tell you
that I was moving out

234
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:45,180
because I didn't want
to hear that from you.

235
00:13:46,990 --> 00:13:47,730
What are you saying?

236
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:49,360
I'm a grown-up.

237
00:13:49,850 --> 00:13:51,520
I can buy my own house.

238
00:13:51,610 --> 00:13:53,720
You don't have to worry about me anymore.

239
00:13:54,070 --> 00:13:54,950
You don't have

240
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:56,670
to bend over backward to look after me.

241
00:13:57,240 --> 00:14:00,230
I'm worried about you.
It's my duty to take care of you.

242
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:02,300
We're family.

243
00:14:05,070 --> 00:14:05,730
Are we?

244
00:14:08,370 --> 00:14:10,570
Do you really think of me as your family?

245
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:21,170
Aunt Su-chen,
haven't you thought about it?

246
00:14:23,060 --> 00:14:24,520
The moment I'm of age,

247
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:26,580
I wanted to move out.

248
00:14:27,770 --> 00:14:28,830
Every time you called,

249
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:29,930
I always said,

250
00:14:30,900 --> 00:14:32,960
"I'm busy. Don't disturb me."

251
00:14:33,050 --> 00:14:33,890
Even during this move,

252
00:14:33,980 --> 00:14:35,740
I couldn't bring myself to tell you.

253
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:39,300
It's because I don't want
to see you anymore.

254
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:42,070
Hsieh Tien-ti.

255
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:43,660
Why are you so good to me?

256
00:14:45,330 --> 00:14:47,310
You're always so kind to me,

257
00:14:47,880 --> 00:14:49,240
particularly in front of others.

258
00:14:49,550 --> 00:14:50,210
It's like

259
00:14:50,700 --> 00:14:52,020
you're reminding me

260
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:53,690
that I don't have parents.

261
00:14:53,780 --> 00:14:55,490
My only grandma didn't want me.

262
00:14:55,620 --> 00:14:57,560
You're just pitying me.

263
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:58,830
What are you saying?

264
00:15:02,490 --> 00:15:05,210
I was particularly nice to you
in front of other people?

265
00:15:06,180 --> 00:15:07,410
That I'm pitying you?

266
00:15:10,670 --> 00:15:12,120
Since the first day you came to my house,

267
00:15:12,210 --> 00:15:13,750
when I held your small hand

268
00:15:15,470 --> 00:15:16,700
and when you came to us,

269
00:15:17,310 --> 00:15:19,780
I've treated you like my own daughter.

270
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:21,710
I should be spoiling you right now.

271
00:15:21,850 --> 00:15:22,810
Why would I...

272
00:15:30,650 --> 00:15:32,320
You said I felt sorry for you?

273
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:36,940
But if you really think of me

274
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:39,620
as your own child,

275
00:15:41,210 --> 00:15:42,220
then why

276
00:15:44,510 --> 00:15:46,790
did you want me to call you "aunt"?

277
00:15:47,670 --> 00:15:49,210
You never asked me

278
00:15:50,580 --> 00:15:52,470
to call you "mom."

279
00:16:04,610 --> 00:16:06,330
I was afraid I wouldn't do well.

280
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:13,980
I was afraid I wouldn't be
a good mother to you.

281
00:16:39,020 --> 00:16:39,720
Mom.

282
00:16:44,780 --> 00:16:45,880
I'm sorry.

283
00:17:11,710 --> 00:17:13,430
From now on,

284
00:17:15,540 --> 00:17:17,869
no matter what happens to me,

285
00:17:19,150 --> 00:17:21,609
you won't feel sad for me anymore.

286
00:17:22,670 --> 00:17:23,810
You will only remember

287
00:17:23,900 --> 00:17:26,800
that I said a lot of hurtful things today.

288
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:32,480
No matter what happens in the future,

289
00:17:34,150 --> 00:17:37,400
you'll only regret it a little.

290
00:17:37,490 --> 00:17:40,220
But you won't feel sad for me anymore.

291
00:17:42,820 --> 00:17:45,810
You've done everything you could.

292
00:17:47,260 --> 00:17:48,400
You did your best.

293
00:17:50,300 --> 00:17:51,880
You were a good mother.

294
00:18:25,670 --> 00:18:27,520
That year when my grandma sent me away

295
00:18:29,060 --> 00:18:31,210
and Aunt Su-chen adopted me,

296
00:18:31,350 --> 00:18:33,680
it was your doing, wasn't it?

297
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:36,450
Yes.

298
00:18:37,730 --> 00:18:39,310
Why did you choose her?

299
00:18:41,250 --> 00:18:42,920
That's not for me to decide.

300
00:18:44,280 --> 00:18:46,880
I only did it according
to the Reflection of Time.

301
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:50,090
But I understand

302
00:18:50,220 --> 00:18:51,980
why Kakarayan arranged it that way.

303
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:56,210
Because in the Reflection of Time,

304
00:18:56,820 --> 00:18:58,190
I saw how she has been really nice to you.

305
00:18:59,290 --> 00:19:00,780
She raised you like her own.

306
00:19:01,530 --> 00:19:02,980
She has done a lot for you.

307
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:07,600
Yes.

308
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:10,770
She's really nice to me.

309
00:19:12,260 --> 00:19:14,600
When I was little,
it didn't matter what I did wrong.

310
00:19:15,260 --> 00:19:17,240
She always scolded my brother,
never at me.

311
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:20,930
She gave me all the good stuff first.

312
00:19:21,060 --> 00:19:22,470
My brother didn't get to choose.

313
00:19:29,910 --> 00:19:33,210
I guess we weren't meant to be.

314
00:19:34,750 --> 00:19:36,240
We both had so much to say,

315
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:39,980
but we only hid it inside our hearts.

316
00:19:41,130 --> 00:19:43,370
That's why I misunderstood her
for so many years.

317
00:19:45,750 --> 00:19:47,380
But after this,

318
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:51,600
she probably won't be worried
about me anymore.

319
00:19:52,700 --> 00:19:55,600
She can go back to her real family.

320
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:58,550
She won't be heartbroken

321
00:20:00,180 --> 00:20:01,190
if anything happens to me.

322
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:02,860
Am I right?

323
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:10,170
Are you done?

324
00:20:10,910 --> 00:20:12,500
Can I have the comb back?

325
00:20:21,210 --> 00:20:22,000
Right.

326
00:20:23,670 --> 00:20:24,910
I just thought of something.

327
00:20:27,060 --> 00:20:28,730
I have one more favor to ask.

328
00:20:31,550 --> 00:20:33,220
Left hand or right hand?

329
00:20:34,670 --> 00:20:35,250
What?

330
00:20:36,700 --> 00:20:37,450
Pick one.

331
00:20:39,730 --> 00:20:40,480
Left hand.

332
00:20:40,750 --> 00:20:43,430
Okay, let's watch the movie on the right.

333
00:20:43,870 --> 00:20:44,570
It's a romantic movie.

334
00:20:45,450 --> 00:20:46,380
Watch a movie?

335
00:20:46,510 --> 00:20:47,170
Yes.

336
00:20:48,930 --> 00:20:51,660
I realized that I used to only think

337
00:20:52,140 --> 00:20:53,860
about myself.

338
00:20:54,380 --> 00:20:55,310
I never thought

339
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:57,330
about how your life is

340
00:20:58,520 --> 00:21:00,280
as my guardian angel.

341
00:21:12,910 --> 00:21:14,580
So I started imagining

342
00:21:15,500 --> 00:21:17,310
how you spend your life.

343
00:21:18,140 --> 00:21:19,990
I remember what you told me.

344
00:21:20,340 --> 00:21:23,690
You said you can see
the reflection of the future.

345
00:21:26,370 --> 00:21:27,560
I thought

346
00:21:27,690 --> 00:21:29,190
having the ability to foresee the future

347
00:21:29,320 --> 00:21:30,640
was an enviable thing.

348
00:21:31,390 --> 00:21:32,270
Until you showed me

349
00:21:32,360 --> 00:21:35,000
what the future holds,

350
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:39,090
I suddenly realized

351
00:21:40,140 --> 00:21:41,510
that you're quite pitiful.

352
00:21:43,750 --> 00:21:44,720
I'm pitiful?

353
00:21:46,430 --> 00:21:49,650
Yes, it's like you're watching

354
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:51,670
the same movie over and over.

355
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:54,270
You know exactly

356
00:21:54,350 --> 00:21:56,330
what bad things will happen in the future.

357
00:21:56,820 --> 00:21:58,450
But you can't change it.

358
00:21:58,530 --> 00:22:00,910
You can only watch it happen.

359
00:22:01,530 --> 00:22:02,980
So I thought

360
00:22:04,390 --> 00:22:07,950
if for the next few days,

361
00:22:08,260 --> 00:22:09,670
I let you see things

362
00:22:09,800 --> 00:22:12,000
that are different
from the Reflection of Time,

363
00:22:13,050 --> 00:22:14,420
does that mean

364
00:22:15,650 --> 00:22:18,510
I can let you

365
00:22:18,600 --> 00:22:22,250
enjoy a movie you haven't seen today?

366
00:22:25,810 --> 00:22:27,750
I'm smart, aren't I?

367
00:22:30,390 --> 00:22:31,050
Hey.

368
00:22:31,880 --> 00:22:33,340
Let me ask you one thing.

369
00:22:35,010 --> 00:22:37,560
Ever since I remembered you,

370
00:22:37,690 --> 00:22:39,100
I've been feeling confused.

371
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:42,880
Why did you remove my memories of you?

372
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:45,740
Is it because

373
00:22:47,420 --> 00:22:49,130
something happened?

374
00:22:50,320 --> 00:22:51,380
Like an error

375
00:22:51,900 --> 00:22:55,380
that didn't fit the Reflection of Time?

376
00:23:26,570 --> 00:23:27,370
You won't talk?

377
00:23:27,980 --> 00:23:28,820
Forget it.

378
00:23:29,040 --> 00:23:30,530
It doesn't matter what the answer is.

379
00:23:35,290 --> 00:23:36,560
Tomorrow night,

380
00:23:38,590 --> 00:23:40,080
as you said,

381
00:23:40,790 --> 00:23:42,500
it will be the last rainfall, right?

382
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:48,930
You're still not talking?

383
00:23:50,070 --> 00:23:51,210
I guess that's a yes.

384
00:23:56,010 --> 00:23:57,460
Can you tell me

385
00:23:57,550 --> 00:23:59,130
how exactly I'm going to die?

386
00:23:59,880 --> 00:24:00,980
Is it because

387
00:24:01,550 --> 00:24:03,180
of the illness that gave me a fever

388
00:24:03,580 --> 00:24:05,070
and made me pass out?

389
00:24:08,770 --> 00:24:09,160
No.

390
00:24:09,820 --> 00:24:10,440
No?

391
00:24:11,850 --> 00:24:14,000
Why did I die then?

392
00:24:18,360 --> 00:24:21,620
Tomorrow night, you'll be

393
00:24:21,700 --> 00:24:24,870
at the intersection you saw
in the Reflection of Time.

394
00:24:28,220 --> 00:24:29,450
There will be an accident.

395
00:24:30,770 --> 00:24:31,250
An accident?

396
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:37,060
You mean a traffic accident?

397
00:24:40,360 --> 00:24:41,500
You won't say.

398
00:24:42,870 --> 00:24:46,430
My gosh. I can't believe I'd die
in a car accident.

399
00:24:46,520 --> 00:24:48,020
My life is so...

400
00:24:48,150 --> 00:24:48,940
No.

401
00:24:51,580 --> 00:24:53,430
You won't die in that car accident.

402
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:05,610
If you have something to say, just say it.

403
00:25:05,700 --> 00:25:08,430
Don't keep it to yourself.
You'll get sick.

404
00:25:11,910 --> 00:25:12,960
Well?

405
00:25:13,050 --> 00:25:15,120
I'm a great listener.

406
00:25:16,790 --> 00:25:18,290
The girl called you over to her house

407
00:25:18,370 --> 00:25:20,400
the night before she dies.

408
00:25:21,320 --> 00:25:22,550
So she couldn't hold it in anymore

409
00:25:22,690 --> 00:25:24,400
and asked you to spare her life.

410
00:25:24,490 --> 00:25:27,530
"'Orad, please let me live."

411
00:25:27,660 --> 00:25:29,110
She asked me to watch a movie.

412
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:29,990
Watch a movie?

413
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:31,620
Wait.

414
00:25:31,750 --> 00:25:33,600
Is this the time to be watching a movie?

415
00:25:34,210 --> 00:25:34,920
It's true.

416
00:25:37,560 --> 00:25:39,320
It was just a movie.

417
00:25:46,090 --> 00:25:51,550
♫ I don't care if the world falls apart ♫

418
00:25:52,870 --> 00:25:57,970
♫ Who says tomorrow
will be sunny and bright? ♫

419
00:25:59,200 --> 00:26:02,370
♫ The rain will never end ♫

420
00:26:02,590 --> 00:26:05,800
♫ But I won't hold an umbrella ♫

421
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:10,690
♫ So that I can feel your presence ♫

422
00:26:12,400 --> 00:26:15,180
♫ I'm not a god.
I don't have to be generous ♫

423
00:26:15,260 --> 00:26:18,260
♫ Please let me love you selfishly ♫

424
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:23,620
♫ When the souls come together,
I'm no longer afraid of regret ♫

425
00:26:24,550 --> 00:26:27,940
♫ If I went back to the beginning,
what would I choose? ♫

426
00:26:28,020 --> 00:26:31,060
♫ Light a light for me ♫

427
00:26:31,320 --> 00:26:36,070
♫ So that the souls can reunite
and be convinced when they're leaving ♫

428
00:26:37,310 --> 00:26:43,950
♫ Since we crossed paths,
it had to have existed ♫

429
00:26:44,700 --> 00:26:45,400
[Starting today,]

430
00:26:45,530 --> 00:26:47,070
[the southeast air current
carrying high moisture content]

431
00:26:47,210 --> 00:26:48,530
[is getting stronger.]

432
00:26:48,610 --> 00:26:50,290
[The frequency of rain
on Taiwan's main island]

433
00:26:50,420 --> 00:26:52,050
[will subsequently increase.]

434
00:26:52,180 --> 00:26:53,410
[Affected areas are urged to stay alert.]

435
00:26:53,500 --> 00:26:54,820
[There will be thunderstorms
in the afternoon]

436
00:26:54,950 --> 00:26:56,580
[with heavy rainfall.]

437
00:26:56,710 --> 00:26:57,500
[Just a reminder.]

438
00:26:57,590 --> 00:27:00,890
[When you go out,
don't forget your umbrella.]

439
00:27:01,990 --> 00:27:04,100
Wait! That hurts!

440
00:27:04,190 --> 00:27:05,990
No, honey.

441
00:27:06,080 --> 00:27:08,330
I haven't collected the samples.

442
00:27:08,460 --> 00:27:09,950
Please stop pulling. It's not nice.

443
00:27:10,040 --> 00:27:11,270
People are watching.

444
00:27:11,360 --> 00:27:12,070
Let go.

445
00:27:12,200 --> 00:27:13,780
I can really walk.

446
00:27:15,590 --> 00:27:18,930
♫ You connected
the dotted line towards me ♫

447
00:27:19,020 --> 00:27:22,360
♫ I call that yearning ♫

448
00:27:22,490 --> 00:27:28,480
♫ Turns out
I was wide awake in this dream ♫

449
00:27:28,560 --> 00:27:33,890
♫ I don't care if the world falls apart ♫

450
00:27:36,220 --> 00:27:38,420
You won't die in that car accident.

451
00:27:39,870 --> 00:27:42,250
That accident won't take your life.

452
00:27:43,350 --> 00:27:44,710
It will only make you

453
00:27:45,280 --> 00:27:46,870
unable to wake up again.

454
00:27:49,290 --> 00:27:51,180
[Two hours after the accident,]

455
00:27:51,750 --> 00:27:54,220
[you will undergo
a heart transplant operation.]

456
00:27:55,930 --> 00:27:57,380
[A heart transplant?]

457
00:27:59,760 --> 00:28:00,730
[Due to brain death,]

458
00:28:00,820 --> 00:28:03,590
[you'll donate your heart
to another sick person.]

459
00:28:07,110 --> 00:28:08,910
[After the surgery,]

460
00:28:09,620 --> 00:28:11,460
[you are then officially pronounced dead.]

461
00:28:12,780 --> 00:28:15,330
[But thanks to you,
another life will be saved.]

462
00:28:18,990 --> 00:28:22,680
[So if I don't die,]

463
00:28:23,650 --> 00:28:25,890
[what will happen to that person?]

464
00:28:27,040 --> 00:28:28,840
[I can't answer that question.]

465
00:28:30,470 --> 00:28:31,750
Because it won't happen.

466
00:28:33,510 --> 00:28:34,560
What will happen is

467
00:28:36,500 --> 00:28:38,210
[you show up
at the intersection tomorrow.]

468
00:28:39,930 --> 00:28:42,350
[I'll erase all your memories.]

469
00:28:44,640 --> 00:28:45,250
[At least you won't be afraid then.]

470
00:28:45,430 --> 00:28:50,580
♫ I don't care if the world falls apart ♫

471
00:28:51,940 --> 00:28:58,060
♫ Who says tomorrow
will be sunny and bright? ♫

472
00:28:58,450 --> 00:29:01,670
♫ The rain will never end ♫

473
00:29:01,750 --> 00:29:05,180
♫ But I won't hold an umbrella ♫

474
00:29:05,270 --> 00:29:09,190
♫ So that I can feel your presence ♫

475
00:29:09,280 --> 00:29:11,080
Before you erase my memories,

476
00:29:13,590 --> 00:29:16,930
can I ask you one last question?

477
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:21,380
Ask away.

478
00:29:24,060 --> 00:29:27,270
Will there be a next life after death?

479
00:29:36,690 --> 00:29:40,250
I wanted to be cool about it and say,

480
00:29:41,090 --> 00:29:42,360
let's meet in our next lives.

481
00:29:44,480 --> 00:29:45,970
I guess that's not possible.

482
00:29:54,950 --> 00:29:55,520
Hey.

483
00:29:56,050 --> 00:29:57,060
Guardian angel.

484
00:29:59,570 --> 00:30:01,410
This is really the last one.

485
00:30:04,450 --> 00:30:06,390
Can you promise me one thing?

486
00:30:11,490 --> 00:30:12,150
Tell me.

487
00:30:17,690 --> 00:30:18,970
Can you

488
00:30:22,310 --> 00:30:24,030
not erase my memory?

489
00:30:31,030 --> 00:30:33,050
[I don't know when I started]

490
00:30:34,680 --> 00:30:37,320
[to have this feeling.]

491
00:30:39,870 --> 00:30:42,250
[I feel like]

492
00:30:42,820 --> 00:30:45,760
[I've forgotten something]

493
00:30:46,160 --> 00:30:47,480
[that is very, very important to me.]

494
00:30:50,380 --> 00:30:52,190
I've been trying hard to remember.

495
00:30:52,280 --> 00:30:53,770
But I can't remember anything.

496
00:30:57,420 --> 00:30:58,480
[Until...]

497
00:31:01,300 --> 00:31:02,440
[I met you again.]

498
00:31:09,880 --> 00:31:11,640
Then I remembered

499
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:14,940
[the important thing]

500
00:31:15,070 --> 00:31:19,290
[that I've been looking for.]

501
00:31:28,440 --> 00:31:33,990
[Xiexing Store]

502
00:31:49,390 --> 00:31:50,790
I don't want

503
00:31:52,910 --> 00:31:54,490
to forget you again.

504
00:32:02,500 --> 00:32:04,430
Thank you for telling me.

505
00:32:05,670 --> 00:32:07,510
Knowing about the future

506
00:32:07,600 --> 00:32:09,270
that has already been decided

507
00:32:10,150 --> 00:32:11,830
allowed me to decide for myself.

508
00:32:13,630 --> 00:32:15,260
I'm not just a pawn

509
00:32:16,930 --> 00:32:18,870
in this game controlled by fate.

510
00:32:57,230 --> 00:33:00,220
Is this the afterlife?

511
00:32:57,800 --> 00:33:28,470
[Next episode]

512
00:33:00,970 --> 00:33:01,900
[Kakarayan offers]

513
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:03,300
[the kind of run-of-the-mill blessing]

514
00:33:03,390 --> 00:33:04,930
[that you don't have to pay a price for.]

515
00:33:05,020 --> 00:33:06,210
[But I'm offering a chance.]

516
00:33:06,300 --> 00:33:08,060
[A chance to love them again.]

517
00:33:16,940 --> 00:33:18,570
[I can't see the Reflection of Time.]

518
00:33:18,700 --> 00:33:19,890
[Did this happen]

519
00:33:19,980 --> 00:33:21,520
because of me?

520
00:33:21,610 --> 00:33:23,940
[You've almost lost all your powers.]

521
00:33:24,030 --> 00:33:24,950
[Does that mean]

522
00:33:25,040 --> 00:33:26,970
[you are no longer a Kawas?]

523
00:33:31,020 --> 00:33:34,010
[2016, It's a promise]

524
00:33:38,850 --> 00:33:40,480
Thank you.

525
00:33:41,850 --> 00:33:44,350
I was thinking of getting some rice balls.

526
00:33:44,570 --> 00:33:46,290
But I'm so tired.

527
00:33:47,210 --> 00:33:48,180
Eat slowly.

528
00:33:48,270 --> 00:33:48,800
Okay.

529
00:33:55,440 --> 00:33:56,980
Can I ask you a question?

530
00:33:57,070 --> 00:33:57,820
What is it?

531
00:33:59,010 --> 00:34:00,150
I've thought

532
00:34:00,940 --> 00:34:02,440
about this question many times.

533
00:34:02,530 --> 00:34:03,670
But no matter what I think,

534
00:34:03,760 --> 00:34:05,080
it feels strange.

535
00:34:06,920 --> 00:34:08,510
This ring.

536
00:34:08,639 --> 00:34:09,340
You put it on for me

537
00:34:09,429 --> 00:34:10,800
when I was little, didn't you?

538
00:34:12,070 --> 00:34:13,960
So the ring was given to me
when I was little.

539
00:34:14,230 --> 00:34:15,770
I'm all grown up now.

540
00:34:16,250 --> 00:34:19,020
Why is it that I can still wear it?

541
00:34:20,960 --> 00:34:23,420
Is it because you secretly switched it

542
00:34:23,560 --> 00:34:25,540
when I was sleeping?

543
00:34:27,030 --> 00:34:29,139
This ring is no ordinary ring.

544
00:34:30,110 --> 00:34:31,780
It is a promise between us.

545
00:34:33,190 --> 00:34:34,030
A promise?

546
00:34:35,520 --> 00:34:37,020
As long as I'm by your side

547
00:34:37,110 --> 00:34:38,429
and I'm still your guardian angel,

548
00:34:38,870 --> 00:34:41,070
this ring will always be on your finger.

549
00:34:44,719 --> 00:34:45,380
Is that true?

550
00:34:45,949 --> 00:34:46,699
You don't believe me?

551
00:34:47,800 --> 00:34:49,159
Take it off then.

552
00:35:03,730 --> 00:35:04,690
Where is it now?

553
00:35:17,850 --> 00:35:24,140
[Mountain Travel]

554
00:35:18,250 --> 00:35:19,130
One more time?

555
00:35:20,140 --> 00:35:20,890
Take it off.

556
00:35:21,020 --> 00:35:21,590
It's fine.
